# Antelope Dev Style

Write CDT contracts like `takeiteasy.hpp`, `invitono.cpp`, `loot.cpp` / `loot.hpp`, and self-contained integration headers like `alcorswap_interface.hpp`. This is contract WASM style, not node/spring C++.

## Files

- Contract header: `#pragma once`, eosio includes, `class [[eosio::contract("name")]] name : public contract`.
- Contract source: `#include "name.hpp"` then implementations. No logic-only headers without a matching `.cpp` for non-trivial actions.
- Third-party ABI mirrors: include guards, `namespace`, eosio headers only — no vendor internals.

## Shape

- Public: `using contract::contract;`, `ACTION` decls, `[[eosio::on_notify("*::transfer")]]` handlers, `action_wrapper<"action"_n, &contract::action>` for each public action, static `get_supply` / `get_balance` when this is a token.
- Private: `TABLE` rows, `typedef` / `using` multi_index / singleton, helpers.
- Params: `const name&`, `const asset&`, `const string&`, `const symbol&` (and same for other fat types).
- Names: actions snake_case matching ABI; tables `"tablename"_n` (≤12 chars); row types `foo` or `foo_s`; indexes `foo_t` / `foos`; secondary `by_*()` + `indexed_by<"byname"_n, const_mem_fun<...>>`; constants `static constexpr` UPPER_SNAKE.

## Action body (always this order)

1. Auth (`require_auth` / `has_auth` / app permission).
2. `is_account` and token/NFT existence (`stat` `require_find`, template exists).
3. Table reads + invariant `check`s.
4. `emplace` / `modify` / `erase`.
5. Inline `action(...).send()` last.

Upsert: `find` then `emplace` or `modify`. RAM payer is explicit: `user`, `get_self()`, or `same_payer`. Field order on live tables is ABI — never reorder or change types on tables that already hold rows.

```cpp
ACTION loot::addtemplates(const name& user, const uint32_t& template_id, const name& collection, const asset& timeunit_rate) {
    check(has_auth(user) || has_auth(get_self()), "⚡️ Missing authorization by user.");
    config_t config_tbl(get_self(), get_self().value);
    auto config_itr = config_tbl.find(collection.value);
    check(config_itr != config_tbl.end(), "⚡️ Collection config not found.");
    template_t template_tbl(get_self(), get_self().value);
    auto row = template_tbl.find(uint64_t(template_id));
    if (row == template_tbl.end()) {
        template_tbl.emplace(get_self(), [&](auto& r) { r.template_id = template_id; r.collection = collection; r.timeunit_rate = timeunit_rate; });
    } else {
        template_tbl.modify(row, get_self(), [&](auto& r) { r.timeunit_rate = timeunit_rate; });
    }
}
```

